              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Landice L7 Pro Sports</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,829 + $399 delivery (Landice, 27 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20 x 58 in., 400 lb, non-folding</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime frame and parts, 1 yr labour</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">None</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Landice M2 Genesis</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,199 + $299–$599 (Landice, 27 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">21 x 62 in., 300 lb, folding</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime frame, 10 yr parts</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">None</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sole TT8</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,899.99, out of stock (Sole, 22 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 x 60 in., non-folding</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime frame and motor (Sole)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">None</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sole F89</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$2,699.99 (Sole, 22 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">24 in. touchscreen, 375 lb, folding</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime frame and motor (Sole)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">None</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Horizon 7.8 AT</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$1,999 (Horizon, 23 Nov)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 x 60 in., 375 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime frame and motor (Horizon)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">None</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">NordicTrack Commercial 2450</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $2,299 Black Friday ($2,999 list), Nov 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">24 in. touchscreen, 0–14 mph</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime motor advertised</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">iFIT Pro optional, $396 a year</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">NordicTrack X24</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">About $2,999 Black Friday ($4,299 list), Nov 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Incline trainer, −6% to 40%, 24 in. touchscreen</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime motor advertised</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">iFIT Pro optional, $396 a year</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            On paper the rivals win on features per dollar. A <a href="/horizon-7-8-at-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>Horizon 7.8 AT</a> has a wider and longer deck than the
            L7 for less than half its delivered price, and a Sole TT8 gives a non-folding 22 by 60-inch deck for
            about $2,330 less than an L7 Pro Sports before delivery. A NordicTrack Commercial 2450 with five years of
            iFIT Pro comes to about $4,279, still under a delivered L7, with a big screen and classes the Landice
            does not have.
          </p>
          <p>
            What the extra money buys is the warranty and the build. Landice covers parts for life on the L7 and L8,
            not just the frame and motor, and it installs every machine through a dealer who also services it.
            Its frames are the ones it sells into clubs and clinics. If you will use a treadmill hard for 15 or 20
            years, that is a reasonable thing to pay for; if you want screen-led workouts or the most deck for the
            money, it is not. Our <a href="/how-much-does-a-sole-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Sole</a>, <a href="/how-much-does-a-horizon-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon</a> and <a href="/how-much-does-a-nordictrack-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">NordicTrack</a> price guides have every model and
            date behind these figures, and our <a href="/treadmills-over-2500/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmills over $2,500</a> roundup
            covers the premium field.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="used" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>What a Used or Remanufactured Landice Costs</h2>
<p>
            Landice frames last, so used ones hold their value. The clearest dated prices we found were at Fitness
            Superstore, a California dealer, on 27 November 2026:
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[520px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead><tr><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Remanufactured model</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Price (27 Nov)</th><th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Status</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Landice L7 Pro Sports Trainer</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,799</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">In stock</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Landice L9 (older club model)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,799</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">In stock</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Landice L8</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$3,899</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sold out</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The store’s banner offered 5% off remanufactured stock with the code BF5 until 30 November, which would
            bring the L7 to $3,609.05. Our <a href="/how-much-does-a-used-treadmill-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">used treadmill cost guide</a> recorded on 25 November that its warranty page stated a 1-year parts and on-site labour warranty on all
            remanufactured machines. Against a new L7 Pro Sports at $4,829 in Landice’s cart, the rebuilt one saves
            about $1,000 to $1,200, but gives up the lifetime parts warranty, which only covers the original owner.
          </p>
          <p>
            For private sales we have no reliable dated prices, so price any used Landice against those figures:
            a private seller asking close to $3,800 for an older L7 is asking dealer money without the dealer’s
            warranty or delivery. Out of warranty, parts are available: on Amazon on 27 November third-party sellers
            listed a replacement L7 walking belt at $189.99, motor brushes for the L7, L8 and L9 at $39.95 and a Pro
            Sports Trainer display console at $153.29. Use our <a href="/used-treadmill-buying-checklist/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">used treadmill checklist</a> before you pay.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="cheapest" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>When Is a Landice Cheapest?</h2>
<ul>
            <li><strong>Now, to 3 December 2026.</strong> The checkout discount of $600 to $1,000 on the L7 and L8,
            and $800 on the M2, is the largest price cut we have recorded on Landice’s own store. It ends after Cyber
            Monday.</li>
            <li><strong>During delivery or accessory promotions.</strong> The autumn offer of free shipping, delivery
            and installation plus a free orthopedic belt was worth $724 on an L7 with that belt, more than the
            Black Friday cut on a Pro Sports. If you want the orthopedic belt with the basic console, that kind of
            offer is the one to wait for.</li>
            <li><strong>From a dealer, on commercial models.</strong> The Fitness Store’s L7-90 Club at $4,999 was
            $430 under Landice’s own L7 Club price. Ask local dealers for floor models too, but remember they carry
            five years of parts cover, not lifetime.</li>
            <li><strong>With the console you need, not the one on display.</strong> Choosing Pro Sports over Elite
            saves $1,400 on an L7 in the Black Friday cart and $1,800 at list.</li>
            <li><strong>Remanufactured.</strong> About $3,800 for a rebuilt L7 or L9 at Fitness Superstore, with a
            1-year warranty.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The M2 Genesis at $3,199 is the cheapest new Landice, but it is a different machine: steel frame,
            300 lb rating and a 10-year parts warranty rather than lifetime. If you want a Landice for its build and
            warranty, the L7 Pro Sports at $4,829 is the real entry point; if you mainly want a folding treadmill
            with a large screen, compare the M2 with the rivals in the table above first.
          </p>
        </div>


        <!-- Common mistakes -->
        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Where People Go Wrong When Pricing a Landice Treadmill</h2>
          <p>A Landice is expensive, and most of the ways to overpay come from the configuration and the policies, not the headline price.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Comparing the base price with a fully optioned quote</h3>
              <p>An L7 runs from $5,429 to $7,804 at list depending on console, belt and mount. Compare the same configuration at Landice and a dealer, and work out the delivered price, including the $399 delivery and installation.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Paying for the Elite when you will watch your own screen</h3>
              <p>The Elite touchscreen adds $1,400 over the Pro Sports on an L7 in the Black Friday cart and has a 3-year console warranty, against 5 years on the other consoles. If you will use a tablet or TV, choose Pro Sports or Achieve.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Ordering before trying one</h3>
              <p>Landice accepts no returns after delivery and charges 25% to cancel once the treadmill has shipped. Walk on an L7 and an L8 at a dealer, at your real pace, before you order.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Assuming a used or floor-model Landice keeps the lifetime warranty</h3>
              <p>The warranty covers the original owner only, and floor or demo units sold more than a year after manufacture get five years on parts. Price a used or floor unit against that, not against a new order.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- The bottom line -->
        <div id="bottom-line" class="ed-bottomline">
          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">A Landice treadmill costs $3,999 to $8,904 at list, and $3,199 to $7,904 in this week’s sale.</strong> On 27 November 2026 Landice’s cart priced the L7 from $4,829 and the L8 from $5,729 with the Pro Sports
            console, and the folding M2 Genesis at $3,199. Delivery and installation added $399 on the L-Series and
            $299 to $599 on the M2. The sale runs to 3 December.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">Choose the console carefully and try before you buy.</strong> The console moves an
            L7 by up to $1,400 in the sale, returns stop at delivery, and the lifetime parts warranty depends on dealer
            installation. For most home buyers the L7 Pro Sports or Achieve is the configuration to price first; see our <a href="/landice-l7-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Landice L7 review</a> before you order.
          </p>
        </div>

