        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much does a Landice treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Landice’s store on 27 November 2026 the M2 Genesis listed at $3,999, the L7 at $5,429 to $7,804 and the L8 at $6,329 to $8,904, depending on console, belt and mount. Its Black Friday checkout discount brought the M2 to $3,199, the L7 to $4,829 and the L8 to $5,729 with the basic console. Delivery and installation added $399 on the L7 and L8.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is a Landice L7 treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              $5,429 with the Pro Sports console, $5,929 with Achieve and $7,229 with the Elite touchscreen at list on 27 November 2026, or $4,829, $5,129 and $6,229 after the Black Friday discount in the cart. The orthopedic belt adds $325 and the TV mount $250.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is a Landice L8 treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              $6,329 (Pro Sports), $6,929 (Achieve) and $8,129 (Elite) at list on 27 November 2026, or $5,729, $6,129 and $7,129 in the Black Friday cart. The orthopedic belt adds $525 on the L8. It costs $900 to $1,000 more than an L7 with the same console.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Landice have a Black Friday sale?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. On 27 November 2026 Landice’s L7 and L8 pages advertised $1,000 off the Elite, $800 off Achieve and $600 off Pro Sports consoles, and $800 off the M2, applied at checkout from 6 November to 3 December 2026. Club and rehab models were not included.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Landice charge for delivery and installation?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              In Landice’s cart on 27 November 2026, shipping, delivery and installation cost $399 on the L7, L8 and L7 Club. The M2 Genesis cost $299 for curbside delivery or $599 for white glove delivery and assembly. Landice says self-assembly voids the warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Landice warranty really lifetime?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On the L7 and L8 for home use, Landice’s warranty card gives lifetime frame and parts, 5 years on the console (3 on the touchscreen console) and 1 year of labour. It covers the original owner only, and only if a dealer installs it within 60 driving miles of the selling dealer’s store. The M2 has 10 years on parts.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you buy a Landice treadmill on Amazon?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not on 27 November 2026. An Amazon search for Landice treadmills returned only third-party parts and accessories, such as belts, brushes, power cords and lube. Landice sells its treadmills through its own store and authorised dealers.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
